{
  "Shows the steps of a longer task and the user's progress through them. Each step has an indicator and text, with a line between steps, and steps before the current one are marked complete. [Wizard](/wizard) adds a page and navigation buttons to each step.": "",
  "`value` is the current step, identified by its `key` or index, and `x-model` provides two-way binding. Programmatically, use `next()`, `previous()` and `goTo()`, and `onStepChanged` reports the change.": "",
  "Step status": "",
  "Steps before the current one are completed automatically. An item can set `status: 'done'` or `'error'` regardless of the current step, be `optional` or disabled, or show an `icon` instead of its number. Its fields can be functions of your state.": "",
  "Status": "Durum",
  "A step not yet reached, with its number in the indicator.": "",
  "The active step, with `aria-current=\"step\"`.": "",
  "Steps before the current one, and any step with `status: 'done'`. The indicator shows a check, and the line before it is filled.": "",
  "A step with `status: 'error'`. The indicator shows a mark, the text uses the danger color, and it is announced as “Needs attention”.": "",
  "Shows “Optional” below the text. In linear mode, the step can be skipped.": "",
  "An item with `enabled: false`, or a step that linear mode does not reach yet. It has `aria-disabled` and is outside the Tab order.": "",
  "Linear and free navigation": "",
  "`linear` (the default) lets the user reach only completed steps and the next one, while `linear={false}` allows any step. In both cases, `onStepChanging` is raised first. `cancel` keeps the current step, and `promise` waits for a validation or a server response.": "",
  "Orientation": "",
  "One Tab stop: the step focused last, otherwise the current one, otherwise the first reachable step.": "",
  "Left and Right (Up and Down when vertical) move between reachable steps and wrap at the ends. Home and End move to the first and last.": "",
  "Selects the focused step, and `onStepChanging` can cancel it.": "",
  "A `nav` named “Steps” in the kit language, containing an ordered list. If a page has several, give each one its own `label`.": "",
  "A button whose name includes the position, text and status, such as “Step 2 of 4, Address, Where to send it, Completed”.": "",
  "Plain elements with nothing to press. The current step still has `aria-current`.": "",
  "Decorative and hidden from screen readers.": "",
  "The stepper. `data-orientation`, `data-labels`, `data-size`.": "Stepper. `data-orientation`, `data-labels`, `data-size`.",
  "The list and each step with its connector. `data-status` is on the item.": "",
  "The step, as a button or a div. `data-status`, `aria-current`, `aria-disabled`.": "",
  "The circle, the number inside it, the check or error mark, and a custom icon.": "",
  "The line to the next step. `data-status=\"done\"` up to the current step.": "",
  "Units: the step (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `disabled`, `current`, `done`, `error`), its indicator, the mark (`icon` per state), the text and the line (`done`). In a vertical stepper, the line rotates 90 degrees.": "",
  "The indicator, the text and the space around a step, per size.": "Boyuta göre gösterge, metin ve adım çevresindeki boşluk.",
  "The second line, the space between the indicator and text, and the margins and minimum length of the line.": "",
  "The steps in order: `StepperItem` objects (`text`, `description`, `key`, `icon`, `status`, `optional`, `enabled`, `data`) or plain text.": "",
  "The current step, identified by its `key` or index, or `null` for none. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "Lets the user reach a completed step or the one right after the last completed step. Optional steps can be skipped.": "",
  "`horizontal` or `vertical`.": "`horizontal` ya da `vertical`.",
  "In the horizontal orientation, places the text below the indicator (`bottom`) or after it (`end`).": "",
  "`false` makes the stepper display only, with no buttons or Tab stop.": "",
  "Shows the number in the indicator of an upcoming step.": "",
  "Occurs before the current step changes (`from`, `to`, `fromItem`, `toItem`, `byUser`). `cancel = true` keeps it. Setting `promise` to a `Promise<boolean>` waits, and the step changes when it resolves to `true`.": "",
  "Occurs after the current step changes (`index`, `item`, `previous`, `byUser`).": "",
  "The index of the current step, or -1 if there is none.": "",
  "The number of steps.": "",
  "Indicates whether there is an enabled step after or before the current one.": "",
  "Moves to the next or previous enabled step. Returns `false` if there is none or the change was canceled.": "",
  "Moves to a step by index or key, in any order. `onStepChanging` is raised first.": "",
  "`pending`, `current`, `done` or `error`, as displayed.": "",
  "Indicates whether the user can reach the step.": ""
}
